			"Message": "feat(Project): Wire workspace save methods and fix Tauri IPC fallback in Wind\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, and Wind submodules to collectively enable `vscode.workspace.save()` / `saveAll()` / `saveAs()` from extensions and fix two workbench boot crash categories in Wind.\n\n**Mountain (+1 commit, feat):** Add three new IPC handler arms to the Workspace dispatch table in `CreateEffectForRequest` — `Workspace.Save`, `Workspace.SaveAs`, and `Workspace.SaveAll` (including the legacy `saveAll` method name used by gRPC/Client.ts). All three degrade gracefully when Sky has no handler registered, logging a warning and returning the original URI (for Save/SaveAs) or null (for SaveAll) instead of crashing the extension host.\n\n**Cocoon (+1 commit, chore):** Rebuild all 39 `Target/` ESBuild bundles and regenerate the `RouteManifest` to track the four new Mountain RPC methods, raising `MountainMethods` count from 130 to 134 with a generation timestamp of `2026-05-19T22:15:03Z`.\n\n**Wind (+1 commit, fix):** Fix two boot-time crash sources in `ResolveConfiguration` — (1) add `(window as any).__TAURI_INTERNALS__?.invoke` to the fallback chain before the `__TAURI__` variants so the Tauri IPC bridge is found in Tauri v2 webview contexts; (2) replace all `|| undefined` path fallbacks (homeDir, tmpDir, userDataDir, logsPath) with concrete defaults like `/tmp/.fiddee` so `path.posix.join(undefined, 'User')` no longer throws \"The path argument must be of type string\" during workbench initialisation. Propagate the fallback to `extensionsPath` via `userDataDir` so extension scanning never receives undefined.\n\nTogether these changes complete the workspace document save IPC round-trip from Cocoon through Mountain to Sky, while hardening Wind against Tauri version mismatch and missing IPC responses at startup.",
			"SHA": "bbd041b6c55c90b3e0432757dbf463009fc6e181"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T21:53:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Synchronize Cocoon and Mountain submodules\n\nAdvance Cocoon and Mountain to their latest commits, wiring active editor tracking and caching OS property queries.\n\n**Cocoon (+1 commit):** Wire `window.didChangeActiveTextEditor` from Handler.ts into a minimal TextEditor stub derived from URI/languageId, patching `__activeTextEditor` on Context so extensions reading `vscode.window.activeTextEditor` synchronously in `activate()` see the current value. Upgrade `showTextDocument` from a fire-and-forget notification to a `sendRequest` round-trip returning the TextEditor stub from Mountain, with a disposable fallback to prevent crashes when `await`ing and chaining `.selection` or `.revealRange`. Migrate ExtensionSecretStorage from `sendNotification` to `sendRequest` with namespaced methods (`secrets.get`, `secrets.store`, `secrets.delete`) and scoped `extensionId` isolation.\n\n**Mountain (+1 commit):** Cache OS property collection (type, release, arch, CPU topology) and Rosetta 2 detection behind `OnceLock` to eliminate ~10 ms subprocess overhead per IPC call. After document open, call `SetActiveDocumentURI` on application state and fire a fire-and-forget gRPC `window.didChangeActiveTextEditor` notification to keep Cocoon's shim in sync. Refactor `localPty:getTerminalLayoutInfo`/`setTerminalLayoutInfo` to use `GetStorageValue`/`UpdateStorageValue` on StorageProvider, removing manual JSON serialization.\n\nTogether these changes eliminate three extension-host crash categories (synchronous reads of undefined `activeTextEditor`, awaited `showTextDocument` returning undefined, and unhandled secret storage notification rejections) while reducing IPC latency for OS queries and keeping terminal layout persistence simpler.",
			"SHA": "504dc46bc62f73b572c19cfe712435e193eba139"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T21:47:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Synchronize Cocoon, Mountain, Output, and Sky submodules\n\nAdvance four Element submodules to their latest states, incorporating dependency updates, terminal state persistence logic, and build script formatting fixes.\n\n**Cocoon (+2 commits):** Update `@types/node` to 25.9.1 and `protobufjs` to 8.4.0 via Dependabot to align type definitions and protocol buffer runtime with upstream releases.\n\n**Mountain (+1 commit):** Implement terminal layout persistence by wiring `localPty:getTerminalLayoutInfo` and `localPty:setTerminalLayoutInfo` to the `StorageProvider`. This enables the restoration of active terminal tabs and dimensions after window reloads. Additionally, cache the native color scheme detection result in a `OnceLock` to eliminate repeated OS syscalls during boot and focus events.\n\n**Output (+1 commit):** Normalize indentation in `Run.sh` and `prepublishOnly.sh` case statements, replacing mixed tabs/spaces with consistent 0-tab labels and 1-tab branch bodies to adhere to project whitespace standards.\n\n**Sky (+2 commits):** Bump `@astrojs/ts-plugin` to 1.10.9 and `astro` to 6.3.5 via Dependabot to ensure toolchain compatibility.\n\nThese updates restore terminal state across reloads, improve startup performance, and maintain dependency alignment.",
